    /* ── Combined modem NETWORK verdict from its two legs ────────────────
       Single source of truth for "is this modem up?", shared by the table
       cell, the pictorial cards and the drawer.

       Unmasked pair — unchanged both-down rule: either medium up means the
       modem still delivers data, so it is Healthy; only both media down is
       Faulty.

       One leg MASKED (groupHealth reports it as unknown because the parent /
       DFI link is down) — the masked leg proves nothing either way, so the
       verdict comes from the leg that is NOT masked:
           masked + Healthy          -> Healthy   (that leg carries the data)
           masked + Faulty           -> Faulty    (no live path is left)
           masked + masked/unknown   -> N/A       (nothing to judge on)

