        var _siteOk = _selSites.length
            ? function (s) { return _selSites.indexOf(s) !== -1; }
            : function () { return true; };

        var cardLines = (window.json && $.isArray(window.json.mCardLines))
            ? window.json.mCardLines : [];

        /* A CardLine row is a real, configured sensor only when it carries a
   Role or a Multiplication. Rows with BOTH null are unconfigured
   placeholder channels: the API omits them from mAssetInfos, so the
   grid never binds them, and counting them here made the header read
   higher than the grid (35 vs 28 on IPS).

   The test is AND, never OR. Point Machine current/voltage channels
   legitimately carry a Role with Multiplication null (CardLine 111708,
   111709, 111714-111717) and are real sensors that must be counted.

   ADCNumber is deliberately NOT part of this test. A sensor with no
   ADC is still a sensor — it simply has no IoT device behind it. The
   11 IPS MintCard-3/4/5 rows with ADCNumber null and a Role set do
   bind in the grid and must be counted here too. */
        /* A CardLine row is a real, configured sensor only when it carries a
   Role or a Multiplication. Rows with BOTH null are unconfigured
   placeholder channels: the API omits them from mAssetInfos, so the
   grid never binds them, and counting them here made the header read
   higher than the grid (35 vs 28 on IPS).

   The test is OR-keep / AND-skip, never OR-skip. Point Machine
   current and voltage channels legitimately carry a Role with
   Multiplication null (CardLine 111708, 111709, 111714-111717) and
   are real sensors that must stay counted.

   ADCNumber is deliberately not part of this test. A sensor with no
   ADC is still a sensor; it simply has no IoT device behind it. The
   11 IPS MintCard-3/4/5 rows with ADCNumber null and a Role set do
   bind in the grid and are counted here too. */
        /* Count from mAssetInfos, not mCardLines.

